DESCRIPTION:All PCC students are invited to attend a free screening and d
 iscussion of award-winning filmmaker Jon Osaki's newest documentary\, Mak
 ing Waves: The Rise of Asian America. We will be joined by Jon Osaki\, an
 d students will have the opportunity for Q&amp\;A after the screening. Lu
 nch will be provided.Read the description below to learn more about the d
 ocumentary.–Making Waves: The Rise of Asian America explores the vital 
 role of ethnic studies in redefining the narrative and promoting service 
 to communities across the country. From the 1968 student strikes at UC Be
 rkeley and San Francisco State to present-day movements\, Making Waves do
 cuments the stories of Asian American activism and efforts to lift-up eth
 nic studies as a strategy to address present and future anti-Asian hate.W
 ATCH THE TRAILER: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J0IHGV1AEGE (https://ww
 w.youtube.com/watch?v=J0IHGV1AEGE)—Event Details: https://hub.pcc.edu/r
 svp?id=382682 (https://hub.pcc.edu/rsvp?id=382682)
