BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260512T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260512T140000
SUMMARY:Ditch the Script: Real Food\, Real Talk\, Real Men
DESCRIPTION:Old "scripts" about masculinity often force men to hide who t
 hey really are. This leads to isolation—in fact\, 65% of young men feel
  like no one truly knows them. We want to move past those rigid rules to 
 create a space where all of us\, including men\, can be honest\, be thems
 elves\, and build real community.Come join up to 11 other participants to
  enjoy burritos\, share in conversation about masculinity\, learn about P
 CC's Community Art and Technology Studio\, and create your own vinyl shir
 t.Brought to you by PCC's Hope Services and the Margaret Carter Skills Ce
 nter - C.A.T. Studio—Event Details: https://hub.pcc.edu/rsvp?id=383077 
 (https://hub.pcc.edu/rsvp?id=383077)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Old "scripts" about masculinity often force 
 men to hide who they really are. This leads to isolation—in fact\, 65% 
 of young men feel like no one truly knows them. We want to move past thos
 e rigid rules to create a space where all of us\, including men\, can be 
 honest\, be themselves\, and build real community.<br />Come join up to 1
 1 other participants to enjoy burritos\, share in conversation about masc
 ulinity\, learn about PCC's Community Art and Technology Studio\, and cre
 ate your own vinyl shirt.<br />Brought to you by PCC's Hope Services and 
 the Margaret Carter Skills Center - C.A.T. Studio<br />—<br />Event Det
 ails: <a href="https://hub.pcc.edu/rsvp?id=383077" target="_blank">https:
 //hub.pcc.edu/rsvp?id=383077</a>
