SUMMARY:Container Gardening & Small Space Growing Workshop - REGISTRATION
  REQUIRED
DESCRIPTION:Join the PCC Learning Gardens for a container gardening and s
 mall space growing workshop that can serve up to 15 students on Wednesday
 \, May 13\, 2026 from 1:00pm until 2:45pm at the SE campus and 15 student
 s on Thursday\, May 14\, 2026 from 1:00pm until 2:45pm at the Cascade cam
 pus.—Room location will be confirmed after registration has been receiv
 ed.—The workshop will cover the intricacies of growing your vegetables 
 and herbs in containers and small spaces. We will be focusing on starting
  seeds both indoors\, outdoors\, and direct sowing\, sunlight exposure an
 d shading in summer\, successful watering\, soil choices\, trellis buildi
 ng\, pruning/deadheading\, and harvesting. We can also quickly talk about
  overwintering and saving seeds if that interests anyone in the class. Ed
 ucational materials and starter kits will be provided for each student to
  keep and take home. Light snacks will also be provided. Masks are option
 al. Register now\, space is limited!Register now\, space is limited!Regis
 tration link for SE Campus workshop: https://forms.gle/WmqkNrNMawUisxdr6 
