BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260518T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260518T133000
SUMMARY:International Speaker Series
DESCRIPTION:Guest lecture followed by Q&amp\;A  Presentation title: "The 
 EU's Arctic policy – Europe's northern neighborhood"  Summary: The Euro
 pean Union (EU) is in the Arctic through the northern territories of Finl
 and and Sweden\, through the Single Market in Norway and Iceland\, and th
 e EU's partnership with Greenland\, and most recently\, through Canada's 
 participation in Horizon Europe. And most relevantly\, through hundreds o
 f thousands of European citizens who call the Arctic home. The EU has had
  an Arctic policy since 2008\, which is being updated in 2026. What are t
 he areas the EU Arctic policy covers? How does the EU's complex instituti
 onal setting work in the Arctic? How has all this changed since 2022? The
 se are some of the questions this presentation will answer.  Speaker bio:
  Miguel Roncero is a visiting scholar at the Jackson School of Internatio
 nal Studies at the University of Washington\, focusing on the development
  of the blue economy in the Arctic as a way to foster cooperation between
  Europe and North America. A political scientist by education\, Miguel ha
 s been an EU civil servant since 2018\, when he joined the European Commi
 ssion\, the executive branch of the European Union.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Guest lecture followed by Q&amp\;A</p><
 p>  Presentation title: "The EU's Arctic policy – Europe's northern nei
 ghborhood"</p><p>  Summary: The European Union (EU) is in the Arctic thro
 ugh the northern territories of Finland and Sweden\, through the Single M
 arket in Norway and Iceland\, and the EU's partnership with Greenland\, a
 nd most recently\, through Canada's participation in Horizon Europe. And 
 most relevantly\, through hundreds of thousands of European citizens who 
 call the Arctic home. The EU has had an Arctic policy since 2008\, which 
 is being updated in 2026. What are the areas the EU Arctic policy covers?
  How does the EU's complex institutional setting work in the Arctic? How 
 has all this changed since 2022? These are some of the questions this pre
 sentation will answer.</p><p>  Speaker bio: Miguel Roncero is a visiting 
 scholar at the Jackson School of International Studies at the University 
 of Washington\, focusing on the development of the blue economy in the Ar
 ctic as a way to foster cooperation between Europe and North America. A p
 olitical scientist by education\, Miguel has been an EU civil servant sin
 ce 2018\, when he joined the European Commission\, the executive branch o
 f the European Union.</p>
